Yes, the Fibonacci sequence is typically defined as the sum of the previous two numbers. But since the function calls itself, the sequence is generated by adding the previous and current Fibonacci numbers. In this implementation, we use the variable `curr` to keep track of the current number and `prev` to keep track of the previous number. The base case is when the sequence length is 1, where we return the current number. In all other cases, we recursively call the function with the new `curr` and `prev` values. Here is the code in Rail: 

